(2) THE STRUCTURAL REDUCTION:  E[P^m] = sum_{2p+r=m} m!/(p!p!r!) E[h^p B^r]
==============================================================================
   m=1: identity holds: True
   m=2: identity holds: True
   m=3: identity holds: True
   m=4: identity holds: True
   m=5: identity holds: True
   m=6: identity holds: True
   => structural reduction VERIFIED through m=6 at degree 2: True

==============================================================================
(3) THE ALL-DEGREE THEOREM (case B = 0)
==============================================================================
   With B = 0 the sum keeps only r=0, so E[P^{2p}] = (2p)!/(p!p!) * E[h^p].
   Nullcone => E[h^p] = 0 for all p >= 1 => (THM-1570 sB) h = 0 => s*A*C = 0
   => A*C = 0 in the DOMAIN C[s] => A = 0 or C = 0.   ONE-SIDED, ALL DEGREES.

   check the collapse symbolically at B=0:
   m=1 (odd) : E[P^m] = 0   (should be 0)
   m=2 (even): E[P^m] - C(m,p)E[h^p] = 0
   m=3 (odd) : E[P^m] = 0   (should be 0)
   m=4 (even): E[P^m] - C(m,p)E[h^p] = 0
   m=5 (odd) : E[P^m] = 0   (should be 0)
   m=6 (even): E[P^m] - C(m,p)E[h^p] = 0
